// Split out of new_block: its return clause must be a name, and naming
// `ids` and pushing it already fill new_block's own block, leaving no room
// there for push_bterm's call and the length computation too.
new_block2() {
  push_bterm();
  int n = len((import bkind)) - 1;
} return int n;
given cfg_init ():(0) then cfg_nblocks:(1)
given cfg_body_fixture ():(2) then cfg_nblocks:(3)

// How many blocks the graph has. It stays a named reader because a case
// checks it with `then cfg_nblocks`, which docs/TESTS.md requires of any
// function that reads bkind without writing it.
cfg_nblocks() {
  int n = len((import bkind));
} return int n;
given cfg_init ():(0)
given cfg_body_fixture ():(2)
